        'That’s a simple pattern you can use any time: tell God what you need, and thank him for something, both together. Then the promise: “the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts.” A guard stands at the door. Worries may still knock; peace keeps watch.',
        'Then Paul says where to point your mind: “whatever things are true, whatever things are honorable, whatever things are just, whatever things are pure, whatever things are lovely”. In a day full of chores and news and scrolling, that’s a practical choice you can make, a few times a day.'
